OL,3,GNEWSAWhitgift plans will be 'nothing
OL,4,Alike' current site
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe regeneration of a south London
OL,7,Fshopping centre will look "nothing
OL,8,Flike" the existing site, with plans
OL,9,Fincluding up to 4,000 homes, green
OL,10,Fspace and a public square for events.
OL,12,FCroydon Council is scrutinising
OL,13,Fpre-application plans after developer
OL,14,FUnibail-Rodamco-Westfield (URW) bought
OL,15,Fthe ageing Whitgift Centre along with
OL,16,FGreen Park House and the parts of the
OL,17,FAllders building from the John Whitgift
OL,18,FFoundation in July for #31.5m.
OL,20,FThe developer's early proposals
OL,21,Fincluded new details and images of the
OL,22,Fproposed offering.
OL,23,APub: 03-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,326,320,200,140,0,100
